WEBVTT

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.280
Hey, crime lab guy, can you check over here, too?

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.550
Oops, be careful there.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.500
It's no use, I can't get a good reading.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.400
My powers are definitely starting to weaken.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.650
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.380
...the instant I look away.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.520
I just kept counting...

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.960
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:16.330
...that I'd vomited up.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:22.270
In this time that seems so dry,

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:27.380
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:33.240
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.290
...and tears them to pieces.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:45.960
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:53.790
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.410
Keiko Muramatsu, age 23.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.750
After pooling the intel we got from the police and Miss Karasuma,

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:23.350
...we can conclude that she's the one behind this series of attacks on ATMs.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.660
I'll leave you to it.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.720
But be quick about it. We still have a long way to go.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.930
How long do you suppose it will take to hunt them all down?

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.900
Well, judging from this list of targets and the pace we're going...

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.670
Another 30 years, I'd say.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.300
That long?!

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.470
That long.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.310
I guess my life will be nothing but loans and hunts...

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.420
You're not doing any of the hunting.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.450
I just wish the Administrator would narrow down our target list a little.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.690
Like the way he used to...

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.750
Our luck will change for the better soon.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.460
Once I'm back on the front line, our efficiency is gonna shoot up.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.230
Besides, you two aren't gonna be working here for life.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.640
Unlike us hunters...

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.640
Well, it's not that I'm not fond of this job...

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:24.310
But even if you come back to work, Haruto, we still need a replacement.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.190
I think it's about time we faced facts.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.850
Either they were abducted...

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.090
...or have gone into hiding...

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.550
...or were killed.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.390
In any case, Amon and Robin aren't here anymore.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.630
You're one cool customer, Michael...

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.590
You know where it is?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.050
I was just there the other day.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.390
When you get there, follow the instructions of the people there.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:13.890
Sure.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.330
And when you're done, have them treat you to some soba noodles.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.070
Soba?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.130
Yeah. I know you're thinking, "Why soba?" The reason is...

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.230
Are you stepping out, sir?

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.710
Yeah. Just to see Robin off.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.620
I'll just bet. Are you sure you're not heading out to play pachinko?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.740
Um... Care to join me?

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.390
We have a client arriving soon.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:39.980
I wish you'd get your act together.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.450
In the first place, you stood them up last time, so I want you to...

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.400
Ask Robin to help with our hunt?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.070
Yeah, let's have her help us.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.110
Ask Robin...

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.480
Robin rescued me the other day.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.710
But if something like that happened to me again...

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.820
If that sort of thing keeps happening...

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.350
My luck won't hold out forever.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.620
Besides, Miho, aren't you getting close to your limit yourself?

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:17.620
You're planning the hunts yourself and then carrying them out, too...

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.850
I can understand how you want to fill in for Amon,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.300
...but your body won't be able to keep up forever.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.700
And you know how Sakaki is.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.200
Even if he comes back to the hunt, there's no telling if he'll obey you, Miho.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.140
So we should have Robin...

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.110
Put herself in danger?

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.280
If the guys who attacked this place really were after Robin,

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.690
...that will only put her in danger.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.090
I don't think we have to worry about that.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:44.890
Why's that?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.330
Because those guys were after the Orbo.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.890
How can you say that for sure?
We don't even know who they were yet!

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.300
Besides, if they were from Solomon,

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.230
...that would mean that Robin is the target of a hunt.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.740
And if that's the case...

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:11.670
Would you be able to hunt her?

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.720
Could you hunt Robin? Could you do it?

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:29.930
It's all right, we'll see each other again soon.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.300
Really?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.300
Really.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:37.260
Here. Pinky promise, red bean bun promise, chocolate bun promise!

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:42.110
If you're a good girl, that nice girl there says she'll buy you some takoyaki.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:42.840
Okay!

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.490
I guess it's too much to hope for lightning to strike twice...

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:02.830
Bingo!

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.000
Okay, baby, start up!

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.100
Start up! Start up, damn it!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.140
Come on, don't do this to me! Start!

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.570
What am I supposed to do?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.510
You didn't hear from Mr. Nagira?

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.580
No.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.690
All you need to do is baby-sit.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:24.690
Baby-sit?

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:26.350
Yeah, this little girl.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.890
Can these chance encounters be a sign from God?

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.520
Let's go!

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.070
Aw, not again!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.440
You piece of junk!

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.460
H
i
n
o
d
e

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.460
P
l
a
y
g
r
o
u
n
d

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:12.470
Okay, she's all yours for a while.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:28.950
Let's go.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:48.160
Yummy!

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.340
What is it? Would you like some tea?

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.240
I found this big piece inside!

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:02.710
A devil...

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:08.280
Across the sea, there are places where an octopus is called a devilfish.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.520
A "fish of the devil".

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.730
Oh, really?

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:18.370
Okay, you devil! Bad devils like you get eaten up!

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.900
This devil is tasty, though.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.210
There are bad people devils, too.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:28.850
People?

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:33.720
Yeah! My daddy was taken away by devil people.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.780
Taken away?

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:41.390
Mommy says if we stayed in our old house, we'd be taken away by the devils, too.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:45.920
That's why Mommy said that we have to move.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.590
Taken away... by devils...

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.060
This devil is gonna move into my stomach!

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:02.000
That's strange. Why is it so shiny?

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.310
It's just a ball of mud.

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:06.980
It's a dumpling.

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.540
This is called a mud dumpling.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.890
"Dumpling"?

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:17.850
Yep, that's right! It's gonna get lots and lots and lots shinier!

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.530
Shiny, shiny!

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.530
Shiny, shiny!

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:25.500
Shiny, shiny, shiny, shiny!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.640
Shiny, shiny, shiny, shiny!

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.640
That was... Did you do something?

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.030
What did you do just now? What did you do?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.350
No doubt about it.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.580
That was a Witch power just now...

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:48.420
Latent powers.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:51.690
Uncontrollable power that suddenly...

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.860
If I had met this girl just a month ago...

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.600
...I would have hunted her.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:04.800
What's the big idea, making that poor little girl cry?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.680
Dojima...

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:17.220
Mommy! I wanna go back to where Mommy is!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.780
I wanna go back!

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:24.890
I'm sorry.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:28.960
That's better. You have to apologize, Robin.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:30.360
I'm sorry.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:36.330
And next, we make up.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:46.740
All right, good job.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:49.350
That's a good girl, Robin.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:53.720
Now, can you tell me your name?

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:56.760
Minori! Minori Nakayama!

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:00.820
But Mommy said that starting today, I'm gonna be Minori Yoshida!

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.690
Oh, is that right?

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.170
And now, it's time to go on the slides!

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:07.800
Yay, I love the slides!

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.240
Be careful not to trip and fall down, okay?

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.170
"Starting today"?

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.350
I'm guessing that this isn't a normal baby-sitting job, is it?

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:26.950
Well, I'm sure there's a perfectly good explanation.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.460
Like maybe they're being chased by a high-interest loan shark...

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.390
Illegal aliens, maybe? Nah, that can't be it.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:39.430
This job of yours...

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.100
Is it more dangerous than being a hunter?

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:47.440
Well, I'm not gonna pry or anything.

00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:49.670
Dojima...

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.610
Why did you come here?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.650
Why else?

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.950
Because I wanted to see you, Robin.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.220
I was looking around the area where you saved me the other day.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:03.900
And then I suddenly saw you, so I chased after you on your scooter.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.130
But the stupid engine kept dying on me, so l...

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.030
I told you.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.490
Huh? Told me when? Told me what? Where?

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:14.960
I said that if you get mixed up with me, I'd cause you nothing but trouble.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:22.040
I know that, but I really want you to hear me out.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:23.910
I'm begging you.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.910
Come on, think about what I asked you earlier.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:29.910
I know it's a lot to ask, but...

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.110
I can't.

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:38.560
I've thought about it, but I just can't do it.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:44.160
I don't think there's much of a chance that you're being chased by the organization.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:45.520
Why's that?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.770
You hide a tree inside a forest.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.500
That's why you're trying to blend into the crowd, right?

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:57.870
But if Solomon headquarters really wanted to hunt you,

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.480
...I don't think they would've let you run free for a whole month!

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:05.110
I'm begging you. Please. I want you to help us.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:06.580
Give us a hand.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:09.790
Besides, I'm scared.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:13.860
If things go on this way, I...

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.560
But you have to keep going.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:22.970
If you refuse to hunt, you yourself will become the hunted.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.140
Robin...

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:39.680
What should I do?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.170
I'm calling it a day.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.710
Well, hold the fort.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.270
Those two are firm believers in the 9-to-5 workday, aren't they?

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.140
Maybe I'll follow their example.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:10.580
Hi, Miss Karasuma.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:12.380
I'm now tailing the target.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.590
I'll wait for my chance, and then begin the operation on the spot.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:21.170
Wait! It's too dangerous to move alone!

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.360
Meet up with Dojima, and...

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.270
Geez, this again?

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:29.060
She's running off half-cocked again... Why is she in such a hurry?

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.820
Now commencing operation.
Send a request to the Factory.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:51.290
Dammit!

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:52.990
What the hell is Dojima doing?!

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:55.260
I've been calling her for a while now!

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:57.630
Come on, please, I'm begging you!

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.230
Really, I'm begging you!

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:02.870
I'll never ask for anything again! Just this once!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:07.740
I can't do it. In any case, I have to look after this girl.

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:18.080
Looks like her ride is here.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.080
Hold it right there!

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:25.420
I've heard of you people, but you sure aren't what I was expecting.

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:26.920
Come along quietly.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:58.500
That's far enough.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:00.960
Time to go to sleep.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:16.850
Why now...?

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:18.540
This next one is gonna be big!

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.290
You're gonna die!

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.520
'Cause I'm gonna use THIS!

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:44.270
Robin!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.010
Did she say "Robin"?!

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:50.100
Are you serious?!

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:52.040
Did you do that?

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:07.260
Dojima, hunting is YOUR job!

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:08.330
But...

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:44.690
I did it! I did it!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.400
I beat her!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.360
You sure did. Good work, Yurika.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:55.640
So it's true... You're all right.

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:57.610
Yeah.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.680
Looks like you're having a rough time.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:03.490
See? We really do need her.

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:05.680
We need your help, Robin.

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:09.530
The Factory is on their way.

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:11.320
You should go.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:14.590
Right.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:18.060
Thank you.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:19.960
Sure.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:40.920
Fix up my partner, okay?

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:16.460
There's a tradition in Japan where you eat soba noodles when somebody moves.

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.930
I won't ask what you've been up to.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.470
But I won't clean up your messes, either.

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:31.200
If anything ever happens...
Be prepared to accept the consequences.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:41.110
That girl...

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.640
She was a Seed, wasn't she?

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.710
Nagira, do you work to save Witches?

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:54.150
Are you the leader of an organization that opposes the STN or something?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:55.990
I'm done.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:59.090
It's nothing that elaborate.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:01.660
But it's like I told you before, right?

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:07.140
I can't stand people who try to tie other people down, that's all.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.110
So that's why you're helping them.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:13.070
Who knows?

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:17.810
But if that's the case... That means Amon is your enemy.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.230
Maybe he is.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:30.720
Then why did you take me in?

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.240
It's like a bad relationship you can't get out of.

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:35.570
Bad relationship?

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:42.940
Way back when we were kids, we lived together for three months.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.240
Together with Amon...

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:51.050
Yeah.

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:04.200
I helped out on another hunt...

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:11.770
From now on...

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:20.780
What should I do?

00:22:23.490 --> 00:22:24.450
Amon...

00:22:36.970 --> 00:22:44.960
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:47.820
Tell me.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:59.810
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:09.700
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:14.190
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:19.560
...all those promises...

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:25.960
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:31.760
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:40.540
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
